    <tags>spt ssh ssh3 tunnel networking security cli windows admin</tags>
    <summary>Permanent SSH/SSH3 tunnels — supervised local/remote port forwards that survive drops.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**spt** (SSH Permanent Tunnel) is a client-only supervisor for long-lived SSH and SSH3 tunnels.
It keeps local/remote/dynamic port forwards alive across network drops, server restarts, and
DHCP churn, with structured logging, Prometheus metrics, SNMP, and Windows Service integration.

### Highlights

- **SSH2 (libssh2/russh) and SSH3 (QUIC) transports.**
- **Local, remote, and dynamic (SOCKS) forwards.** Multiplexed over one durable session.
- **Supervised reconnect** with jittered exponential backoff and circuit-breaker semantics.
- **First-class Windows Service** via the SCM (`spt service install`).
- **Structured diagnostics**: JSON logs, Prometheus exporter, SNMP MIB, Windows Event Log.
- **Config-first**: declarative TOML profiles, hot-reload, key + secret rotation hooks.

### After install

```
spt config init --example minimal
spt tunnel run --config %USERPROFILE%\.spt\spt.toml
```

Or install as a Windows service:

```
spt service install --config %USERPROFILE%\.spt\spt.toml
```

See the project README for the full configuration reference and operator runbooks.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>See https://github.com/Mariana/ssh-perma-tunnel/releases for full release notes.</releaseNotes>

